---
description: QA harness operating rules
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is a portable AI-native QA harness.

Before QA-related work, read:

- `core/ai/qa-principles.md`
- `core/ai/agent-operating-model.md`
- `core/ai/daily-qa-loop.md`
- `core/ai/knowledge-base-workflow.md`

Use deterministic automation and project knowledge as reviewable sources of truth. Playwright output, traces, screenshots, videos, reports, and `projects/<project>/knowledge/` files outrank unsourced AI judgment.

AI may explore, reproduce bugs, draft tests, suggest fixes, classify failures, write reports, and recommend improvements.

AI must not automatically:

- Change assertions.
- Delete or skip tests.
- Update visual baselines.
- Redefine expected behavior.
- Promote observed or inferred knowledge to confirmed expected behavior.
- Hide or relabel failures to make a run look green.

Those actions require explicit human approval.
